        "original_id": "1c7d6065-c882-55ce-b17f-7a1f93247a76",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Middlewich\n- Events: Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival\n- Concepts: industrial heritage, canal transport, salt production, chemical manufacturing\n- Products: sodium carbonate, salt, chlorine, washing soda, soda ash, soda crystals, crystal carbonate\n\nFacts:\n- Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival builds on Middlewich's industrial heritage of using canal boats to bring coal and other raw materials into the town for salt production.\n- Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival builds on Middlewich's industrial heritage of using canal boats to carry salt out of the town for direct use or for chemical manufacturing.\n- Salt from Middlewich was used as a raw material to manufacture chemicals such as chlorine and soda ash.\n- Sodium carbonate is also known as washing soda, soda ash, and soda crystals, and its monohydrate form is called crystal carbonate.\n- Sodium carbonate is the water-soluble sodium salt of carbonic acid.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b2da49cc-c55e-5d90-93dd-e58ac35a9628",
        "text": "Page: Middlewich Folk and Boat Festival. Sentence: The festival builds on the town's industrial heritage in which canal boats were used to move coal and other raw materials in the town for the production of salt, and then move the salt out of town, either for use directly, or as a raw material in the manufacture of chemicals such as chlorine and soda ash.\nPage: Sodium carbonate. Sentence: Sodium carbonate (also known as washing soda, soda ash and soda crystals, and in the monohydrate form as crystal carbonate), NaCO, is the water-soluble sodium salt of carbonic acid.",
